course: dictionary
lesson: 7178
title: Persistent: keeps on going
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Persistent is an adjective with two main meanings. A persistent person keeps on trying and does not give up easily. Something persistent goes on for a long time or keeps coming back, like rain or a cough.
explain: Use the words around it to choose the meaning. «See a doctor if you have a persistent cough.» A cough that keeps coming back and will not go away is the clue. Try your meaning in the sentence: "See a doctor if you have a cough that keeps coming back" still makes sense.
explain: Persistent can also be used in a negative way. «Persistent abuse can be reported» in online games means unkind behaviour that keeps happening again and again. A persistent salesman who will not leave you alone is annoying, so the context shows you how the word feels.
fact: Persistent means keeps on going, or keeps coming back.
fact: A persistent person keeps trying and does not give up easily.
fact: Persistent can describe something that lasts a long time, such as «persistent rain».
fact: Persistently is the adverb form: it means in a way that keeps going on.
fact: Persistent can sound good or bad: a persistent learner is praised, but a persistent salesman can be annoying.
exercise: «See a doctor if you have a persistent cough.» What does persistent mean here? | A cough that is very loud | *A cough that keeps coming back | A cough that makes you laugh
exercise: Ms Patel says, «Mia is a persistent learner.» What does she mean? | *Mia keeps trying and does not give up easily | Mia never does any work | Mia is very quiet in class | Mia is often late for school
exercise: Which word means someone who keeps trying and does not give up easily? | sleepy | nervous | *persistent | careless
test: «Persistent rain» means rain that | is very warm | is very bright | *keeps falling for a long time | stops very quickly
test: Which sentence uses persistent in a negative way? | The persistent learner finished her project early | Our persistent teacher helped me with my maths | *The persistent salesman kept calling after we said no | The persistent runner trained every morning
exam: Which best describes persistent? | Happy and kind | Late and tired | Very small and quiet | *Keeps going, or keeps coming back
